/-! Diagram volumes of paper A §2 (l.115-118) and A Lemma 3.4 (l.270-276).
Vertices `Fin (n+1)` = `{0,…,n}` (the paper's `{0,…,n-1}` with `n` shifted by one), vertex `0` pinned at the
origin, the other `n` points free in `(ℝ²)ⁿ` — the same layout as `HardDiskB5.Lean.virialB`
(`mayerWeight G x = (-1)^{|E(G)|} * contactWeight G ⊥ x`).
`V_{H,F} = ∫ ∏_{ij∈H} 1[|x_i-x_j|<1] ∏_{ij∈F} 1[|x_i-x_j|≥1]`, `V_H = V_{H,∅}`;
`Vpin H F i j p` = the same product without the factor of `ij`, with `x_i = 0`, `x_j = p`, integrated over the
other points; `V^{ij}_{H,F} = Vpin H F i j e` (`|e| = 1`), the lens functional of A Prop 3.1 is `Vpin H ⊥ i j (λ e1)`.
Integrands are products of indicators of open/closed sets (bounded, measurable); for connected `H` the
support is bounded (every point is joined to a pinned point by edges of length < 1), so the integrals are
of bounded compactly supported functions. For disconnected `H` the integral is not finite and the Bochner
value is 0 — every statement using `VHF`/`Vpin` either assumes `H` connected (as printed) or uses graphs
that are connected. -/

